
  <sn><md>### Network Topologies

**Network topology** refers to `the arrangement (physical or logical) of devices and connections` in a network. It determines how data flows between nodes.

![img](https://www.dnsstuff.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/08/network-topology-types-1024x536.png)
</md></sn>
